  "title": { "en": "Daily routine", "uz": "Kundalik tartib", "ru": "Распорядок дня", "tr": "Günlük rutin" },
  "goal": {
    "en": "Talk about your day and say how often you do things.",
    "uz": "Kuningiz haqida gapiring va ishlarni qanchalik tez-tez qilishingizni ayting.",
    "ru": "Расскажите о своём дне и о том, как часто вы что-то делаете.",
    "tr": "Gününü anlat ve bir şeyleri ne sıklıkla yaptığını söyle."
  },
  "guide": "everest",
  "color": "#2563EB",
  "tip": {
    "title": { "en": "I work, she works", "uz": "I work, she works", "ru": "I work, she works", "tr": "I work, she works" },
    "body": {
      "en": "For habits use the simple verb: I get up at seven. With he, she or one person add -s or -es: She works. He goes. In questions and negatives the -s moves to \"does\": Does he work? She doesn't work. Always, usually, sometimes and never go before the verb (I always get up early) but after am, is, are (She is never late). With \"never\" do not add \"not\": I never drink coffee.",
      "uz": "Odatlar uchun fe'lning oddiy shakli ishlatiladi: I get up at seven. He, she yoki bitta odam bilan -s yoki -es qo'shiladi: She works. He goes. Savol va inkorda -s \"does\"ga o'tadi: Does he work? She doesn't work. Always, usually, sometimes, never fe'ldan oldin turadi (I always get up early), lekin am, is, are dan keyin keladi (She is never late). O'zbek tilidan farqli, \"never\" bilan yana inkor qo'shilmaydi: I never drink coffee (Men hech qachon qahva ichmayman).",
      "ru": "Для привычек используется простая форма глагола: I get up at seven. С he, she или одним человеком добавляется -s или -es: She works. He goes. В вопросе и отрицании -s переходит к \"does\": Does he work? She doesn't work. Always, usually, sometimes, never стоят перед глаголом (I always get up early), но после am, is, are (She is never late). В отличие от русского, с \"never\" второе отрицание не нужно: I never drink coffee (Я никогда не пью кофе).",
      "tr": "Alışkanlıklar için fiilin yalın hâli kullanılır: I get up at seven. He, she ya da tek bir kişiyle -s veya -es eklenir: She works. He goes. Soruda ve olumsuzda -s \"does\"a geçer: Does he work? She doesn't work. Always, usually, sometimes, never fiilden önce gelir (I always get up early), ama am, is, are'dan sonra gelir (She is never late). Türkçeden farklı olarak \"never\" ile ayrıca olumsuzluk eklenmez: I never drink coffee (Asla kahve içmem)."
    },
    "examples": [
      { "en": "I get up at seven.", "native": { "uz": "Men soat yettida turaman.", "ru": "Я встаю в семь.", "tr": "Ben saat yedide kalkarım." } },
      { "en": "She works every day.", "native": { "uz": "U har kuni ishlaydi.", "ru": "Она работает каждый день.", "tr": "O her gün çalışır." } },
      { "en": "I never drink coffee.", "native": { "uz": "Men hech qachon qahva ichmayman.", "ru": "Я никогда не пью кофе.", "tr": "Ben asla kahve içmem." } }
    ]
  },
